Thanks @phcorp, I pushed the changes from my review, squashed and rebased. The grapheme pattern is now copied in the package. Without polyfill-intl-grapheme, `😀😀` was one character on PCRE < 10.44. The data are pinned to Unicode 17.0.0, like IntlChar. Long ZWJ sequences don't exhaust the PCRE stack anymore, and `following()` doesn't move backwards on stray continuation bytes. I also updated the description, with numbers for PCRE 10.42.

